class:: MFCC2
summary:: Configurable Mel-frequency cepstral coefficients
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/MFCC, Classes/SpecCentroid2

description::
Integrates an FFT spectrum through triangular Mel filters, applies a natural logarithm, then a DCT-II. The output count, band count, coefficient zero, frequency bounds, Slaney/HTK Mel mapping, magnitude/power input, DCT normalization, and liftering are explicit initialization choices. Silence deterministically produces the DCT of the configured log floor rather than NaN or Inf.

The implementation follows the standard paper-defined MFCC pipeline and shares MIRa's tested filter-bank and DCT kernels. It is practically similar to link::Classes/MFCC::, but removes its fixed historical representation and undocumented output scaling; numerical identity is not expected.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize::.

argument:: numCoeffs
Literal output count from 1 through 64.

argument:: numBands
Literal Mel band count from 4 through 128 and large enough for the requested coefficients.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest Mel-filter edge in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest Mel-filter edge in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: include0
Nonzero begins at coefficient 0; zero begins at coefficient 1.

argument:: melMode
Literal code::\slaney:: or code::\htk::.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 integrates magnitude and 1 integrates power.

argument:: logFloor
Positive energy floor before the natural logarithm.

argument:: dctNorm
Nonzero uses orthonormal DCT-II scaling.

argument:: lifter
Positive sinusoidal lifter length; 0 disables liftering.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
An Array of code::numCoeffs:: control-rate outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::
Thirteen Mel-frequency cepstral coefficients capture spectral envelope shape and vocalic formant contours. In this example, 13 coefficients dynamically shape a vocoder carrier bank: low coefficients steer overall spectral tilt while higher coefficients imprint detailed vowel formants onto an analog pulse synthesizer. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.bars:: displays the real-time MFCC spectrum.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 13);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var mfcc = MFCC2.kr(chain, 13, 40, fftSize: 1024);
        var carrier = Pulse.ar([110, 220], 0.3).sum;
        var filtered = BPF.ar(carrier, mfcc.copyRange(1, 4).tanh.linexp(-1, 1, 300, 3200).lag(0.04), 0.15).sum;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + (filtered * 0.25);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, mfcc) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.bars("MFCC Coefficients", ~miraBus, 13, -40, 40);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
